t_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause** (in `pricing/money.py`):\n- The float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` treats it as below the halfway point and rounds down.\n- `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. That breaks the \"half up\" behaviour the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts `repr(x)` to a `Decimal` and rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. `repr` gives the shortest decimal that maps back to the same float (`\"2.675\"`, not `\"2.67499999\u2026\"`). So the halfway check is made on the number the customer sees. It still returns a `float`, so `add_vat` and other callers are unaffected. Negative values round half away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`).\n\n**Checks:**\n- With the old code, `round(2.675,2)`, `round(1.005,2)` and `round(0.125,2)` gave `2.67`, `1.0` and `0.12`.\n- I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering those three cases, a negative value and a below-half value. All four tests pass with the fix, and the existing `test_split` still passes.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`. There's no git repo either, so I couldn't stash the fix to confirm the new tests fail without it. The old outputs above are the evidence that they would.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 266205, "requests_cache_write": 26247, "requests_cost_usd": 0.235004, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2522, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed